      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "STREET SKATER (3) dropped in grade for an easier Class 1 and it showed with the margin of victory. This will be hardly a strong Class 2 but maybe he is just better suited back over the shorter distances. There are plenty of chances though. MR CACCIATORE (2) is one of them coming off a maiden win before a spell. He led them up at Bathurst and held on gamely. It could well have been the better surface that helped there. SWEDISH GLITTER (6) is a winner here previously. Can be up and down with form but might be placed. ERION (5) could be one to watch when resuming. Has run some decent races doing that in the past. TAMPA BAY (4) had one start here and that broke her maiden. Should be up on the pace once more.",
